  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "MqttDecode_Props",
    "file": "wolfmqtt/src/mqtt_packet.c",
    "description": "Heap OOB read is caused by MqttDecode_Props not validating that remaining property bytes (prop_len) and buffer bytes are sufficient before decoding each property identifier/value. It calls MqttDecode_Vbi(buf, ..., buf_len - (buf - pbuf)) even when buf has already advanced beyond pbuf+buf_len due to malformed prior length fields, so the computed length underflows (word32) to a huge value and MqttDecode_Vbi reads from an invalid pointer (crash at mqtt_packet.c:232).",
    "conditions": "From the fuzzer path (Connect -> WaitType -> DecodePacket -> MqttDecode_Auth), attacker-controlled AUTH packet bytes set a properties length and property contents such that MqttDecode_Auth passes a truncated remaining length into MqttDecode_Props, then inside the property loop buf/propery-length accounting becomes inconsistent (no upfront per-field bounds checks). A crafted property sequence can move buf past the real rx buffer while loop still continues, leading to underflow in (buf_len - (buf - pbuf)) and OOB read in MqttDecode_Vbi."
  },
